+FIXED - cluster ci-642b4d09f4421388: the hosted linux-x86_64 (Qt 5) build stops at `QByteArrayView: No such file or directory`
+
+Verdict: FIXED (REAL). The reported error reproduces byte-for-byte on a Qt 5.15
+toolchain. Reproduction then exposed three further Qt-6-only assumptions in the
+same build that stop the same CI job; all four are fixed here, because the
+packet's outcome ("the linux-x86_64 build compiles and its ctest runs green")
+cannot be met with only the first one fixed. Every fix is minimal, verified and
+behaviour-preserving; the script digests are byte-identical before and after.
+
+## The reported failure
+
+Hosted CI `build / linux-x86_64`, train 050/m0-train-27 at `a1a98b67b2`
+(this checkout's HEAD), step Build:
+
+```
+src/core/ControlCommandsScript.cpp:30:10: fatal error: QByteArrayView: No such file or directory
+   30 | #include <QByteArrayView>
+compilation terminated.
+gmake[2]: *** [src/CMakeFiles/lmmsobjs.dir/build.make:2888: .../ControlCommandsScript.cpp.o] Error 1
+```
+
+The job builds the Qt 5 branch: `.github/workflows/build.yml:158` sources
+`/opt/qt5*/bin/qt5*-env.sh` and passes no `-DWANT_QT6=ON` (the Qt 6 jobs pass it
+explicitly, e.g. `quality-gates.yml:157`). `CMakeLists.txt:373` still declares a
+Qt 5.15.0 minimum, so Qt 5 is a supported configuration and the product code
+must compile there.
+
+## Reproduction (Qt 5.15.19, this box)
+
+A second build tree was configured inside the lane worktree (`build-qt5`,
+git-ignored by `/build*/`) with the lane shim's real binary, because the shim
+refuses a top-level configure ("configuring is the parent's job", exit 97) and
+the lane tree is Qt 6:
+
+```
+/usr/bin/cmake -S . -B build-qt5 -DUSE_WERROR=ON -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=RelWithDebInfo \
+  -DTARGET_UARCH=none -DUSE_COMPILE_CACHE=ON -DWANT_DEBUG_CPACK=ON -DWANT_VST3=ON \
+  -DWANT_CLAP=ON -DWANT_VST3_TEST_INSTRUMENT=ON -DWANT_QT6=OFF \
+  -DQt5Svg_DIR=<tmp>/qt5svg-dl/prefix/usr/lib/cmake/Qt5Svg \
+  -DLMMS_VST3_SDK_PATH=<wt>/build/vst3sdk -DLMMS_CLAP_PATH=<wt>/build/clap
+```
+
+(`Qt5Svg_DIR` points at the distro `qt5-svg` package extracted under `$TMPDIR`;
+this box's Qt 5 had no Svg module. `TARGET_UARCH=none` matches the lane tree;
+the CI's `official` is an `-march` flag and cannot change a header lookup.)
